1
00:00:01,330 --> 00:00:04,210
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:00:13,010 --> 00:00:17,430
DAEMONS OF THE SHADOW REALM

3
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:31,970
[traffic passing]

4
00:01:34,590 --> 00:01:36,260
♪

5
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:43,230
Danji, no more lies.

6
00:01:43,350 --> 00:01:44,770
You're not a human, are you?

7
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:47,230
-[Danji breathes shakily]
-[YURU] You're a daemon.

8
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:49,480
All this time,

9
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:52,280
you've lied to me, too.

10
00:01:53,070 --> 00:01:55,160
[DANJI]
And this is my true form.

11
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:56,240
[Ken gasps]

12
00:02:00,330 --> 00:02:03,960
A little boy and girl,
Zashiki-Warashi.

13
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:07,960
[YURU] Kyoka too?
Was everyone lying?

14
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:09,750
That's it.

15
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:12,470
There's not a soul
in the village I can trust.

16
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:14,510
They all want me dead.

17
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:17,430
[inhales]

18
00:02:17,550 --> 00:02:18,760
[sighs]

19
00:02:19,140 --> 00:02:21,140
[dog panting]

20
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:25,060
[Yuru grunts]

21
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:28,150
What do you want?

22
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:31,940
[yelps]
Hey, could you leave?

23
00:02:32,070 --> 00:02:33,360
I've got a lot on my mind,

24
00:02:33,490 --> 00:02:35,410
and I'd kinda like
some time alone!

25
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:37,070
[dog continues panting]

26
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:39,080
Damn mutt won't go.

27
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:40,950
Hmm.

28
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:46,420
There's always too much going on
in the world down here.

29
00:02:46,830 --> 00:02:49,340
I can't get a moment's solitude.

30
00:02:50,250 --> 00:02:51,710
Back in the village,

31
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:54,220
I could go into the mountains
to be alone.

32
00:02:54,470 --> 00:02:57,800
I could think freely
without any interruptions.

33
00:02:58,890 --> 00:03:02,060
Between the bandits,
beasts, and nature itself,

34
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:04,350
the threat of death
is ever present

35
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:05,600
in the mountains.

36
00:03:06,190 --> 00:03:07,690
That made things simple.

37
00:03:08,150 --> 00:03:10,020
Just focus on survival.

38
00:03:10,650 --> 00:03:12,440
What do I need to do
in this moment

39
00:03:12,570 --> 00:03:14,150
to be alive the next?

40
00:03:14,490 --> 00:03:16,280
If I could focus on that,

41
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:18,370
all the noise in my mind
would go away

42
00:03:18,490 --> 00:03:20,120
and I could find answers.

43
00:03:20,740 --> 00:03:22,660
That's why I love the mountains.

44
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:26,040
But there he was. Danji.

45
00:03:26,370 --> 00:03:28,500
Always wanting
to tag along with me.

46
00:03:28,710 --> 00:03:29,790
He'd say,

47
00:03:30,250 --> 00:03:33,050
"What if something bad happens
to you while you're alone?"

48
00:03:33,250 --> 00:03:34,380
[grunts softly]

49
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:37,430
It was so annoying.

50
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:40,390
EPISODE 15
YURU AND DANJI

51
00:03:41,350 --> 00:03:43,010
[bird screeching]

52
00:03:43,140 --> 00:03:45,640
[Yuru (child) cries]

53
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:10,830
[YURU (CHILD)]
Mom and Dad fled the village.

54
00:04:13,290 --> 00:04:16,920
Now Asa and I are all alone.

55
00:04:18,510 --> 00:04:19,970
I can't believe it.

56
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:23,140
They're really gone.

57
00:04:24,470 --> 00:04:26,230
[continues crying]

58
00:04:27,020 --> 00:04:28,520
Well, I'm not.

59
00:04:30,350 --> 00:04:33,900
Now and forever,
I'll stay by your side.

60
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:38,570
[Yuru grunts]

61
00:04:38,690 --> 00:04:39,990
Damn.

62
00:04:42,490 --> 00:04:44,120
I wasn't trying
to think about that,

63
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:45,870
so why'd you
have to remind me?

64
00:04:45,990 --> 00:04:47,700
[dog panting]

65
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:53,380
He told us he didn't want
anyone else there.

66
00:04:53,500 --> 00:04:54,800
[FEMALE DAEMON]
A dog isn't a person.

67
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:56,710
So this doesn't count.

68
00:05:02,930 --> 00:05:04,260
♪

69
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:07,270
[LEFT] 'Tis apparent
why you've taken

70
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:09,100
such a liking to your master.

71
00:05:09,980 --> 00:05:12,600
[female daemon chuckles]
We're all the same.

72
00:05:13,860 --> 00:05:16,730
[gasps] You're getting
a little too friendly.

73
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:19,610
[FEMALE DAEMON]
None of us can live alone.

74
00:05:19,900 --> 00:05:21,490
[footsteps]

75
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:25,370
[YURU] Where's Danji?

76
00:05:25,490 --> 00:05:27,660
The young lad just ran off
by himself.

77
00:05:27,790 --> 00:05:29,540
[MALE DAEMON]
Welcome back, Master.

78
00:05:29,660 --> 00:05:31,290
[RIGHT]
He said he had something to do.

79
00:05:31,410 --> 00:05:32,670
[YURU] What's that?

80
00:05:32,750 --> 00:05:34,710
[LEFT] He appears to have sensed
his other half here

81
00:05:34,830 --> 00:05:35,880
in the outside world.

82
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,920
Wait, you mean the fake Asa?

83
00:05:38,130 --> 00:05:40,050
Did she also come down
the mountain?

84
00:05:40,170 --> 00:05:41,590
He went off to look for her.

85
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:43,470
[YURU] By himself?

86
00:05:43,590 --> 00:05:44,550
But how?

87
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:46,350
[RIGHT] We daemons have
a strong bond

88
00:05:46,470 --> 00:05:48,510
with our other half.
He'll find his way.

89
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:50,350
[LEFT]
Even from great distances,

90
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:52,390
we can divine
each other's location.

91
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:55,650
Still, come on.
He left without saying goodbye.

92
00:05:55,770 --> 00:05:57,820
I had questions I wanted
to ask him.

93
00:05:58,110 --> 00:06:00,240
[KEN] He gave me
a message for you.

94
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,440
He said sorry,

95
00:06:01,570 --> 00:06:04,030
and that he wouldn't be making
any excuses.

96
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:05,450
[YURU] Hm?

97
00:06:05,820 --> 00:06:07,330
-[grunts]
-[dog pants]

98
00:06:07,450 --> 00:06:08,660
[FEMALE AND MALE DAEMON]
Mm. Mm-hm.

99
00:06:08,790 --> 00:06:10,370
[MALE DAEMON]
The sun is starting to go down,

100
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:13,080
so we should leave
before it gets too dark outside.

101
00:06:13,210 --> 00:06:14,330
Aye, so long.

102
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:17,580
[FEMALE DAEMON] We like
hanging out around this area.

103
00:06:17,710 --> 00:06:20,340
Feel free to contact us anytime.

104
00:06:20,460 --> 00:06:22,920
Great, thank you! [chuckles]

105
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:27,390
It's so nice talking to daemons
who don't want to eat me!

106
00:06:27,510 --> 00:06:29,010
[all grunt]

107
00:06:31,850 --> 00:06:33,520
[FEMALE DAEMON] Mr. Danji.

108
00:06:35,940 --> 00:06:38,270
[MALE DAEMON] You're looking
for your other half, right?

109
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:39,480
-Let us help.
-Oh, no,

110
00:06:39,650 --> 00:06:41,740
I would hate for you
to go to any trouble for me.

111
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:42,940
[FEMALE DAEMON]
It's no trouble.

112
00:06:43,110 --> 00:06:44,650
[MALE DAEMON] We spend
a lot of time around here,

113
00:06:44,780 --> 00:06:45,950
so we know the area.

114
00:06:46,070 --> 00:06:47,490
If we put our talents together,

115
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:49,660
we're sure to find them
before long.

116
00:06:49,780 --> 00:06:50,990
Besides...

117
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:52,580
[FEMALE DAEMON]
We love to make friends

118
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:54,410
with even more living legends
like yourself.

119
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:56,330
[MALE DAEMON]
You're a Zashiki-Warashi!

120
00:06:56,460 --> 00:06:58,380
That's, like, a celeb!

121
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:01,880
[FEMALE DAEMON]
Where shall we start?

122
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,840
[MALE DAEMON]
We'll show you the way.

123
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:05,090
[Danji (tsugai) cries]

124
00:07:05,220 --> 00:07:07,090
[MALE DAEMON] Oh, no!
What's going on?

125
00:07:07,220 --> 00:07:09,350
Why are you crying?
What happened?

126
00:07:09,470 --> 00:07:13,060
[overlapping chatter]

127
00:07:14,020 --> 00:07:15,560
[horse neighs]

128
00:07:17,140 --> 00:07:18,400
What's going on?

129
00:07:18,860 --> 00:07:20,400
Did I miss the invite?

130
00:07:21,230 --> 00:07:22,650
[HANA] Oh, hey, Dera.
Welcome back.

131
00:07:22,770 --> 00:07:25,570
Wow. You had a beard
last time we met, didn't you?

132
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:29,120
Hello, Oshirasama.
What brings you to our home?

133
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:30,320
I took the highway.

134
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:32,370
I didn't mean
what literally brought you.

135
00:07:32,490 --> 00:07:34,790
And horses are considered
motorless vehicles,

136
00:07:34,910 --> 00:07:36,960
so they aren't allowed
to be on highways.

137
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:39,500
My goodness!
We broke traffic laws!

138
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:41,380
[DERA] Hmm? What?

139
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:44,090
You finished the hot pot
without me!

140
00:07:44,210 --> 00:07:46,050
-[cries]
-Thank you for the meal.

141
00:07:46,170 --> 00:07:47,340
Why, Yuru!

142
00:07:47,470 --> 00:07:49,470
Didn't you say we'd eat
together as a family?

143
00:07:49,590 --> 00:07:51,430
Well, Hana told me.

144
00:07:51,550 --> 00:07:53,060
There's no way for us to know

145
00:07:53,180 --> 00:07:54,720
when an emergency
is gonna strike,

146
00:07:54,850 --> 00:07:57,100
so you always need to eat
whenever you get the chance to.

147
00:07:57,230 --> 00:07:58,890
Plus, it was gonna spoil.

148
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:00,360
Thank you for the meal.

149
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:03,110
Seemed like good logic to me.
Yeah?

150
00:08:03,230 --> 00:08:05,280
Yeah, you do make a good point.

151
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:07,990
I should've eaten the hot pot
while I had the chance.

152
00:08:08,110 --> 00:08:10,410
[HANA] Did you not get anything
while you were out?

153
00:08:10,530 --> 00:08:12,910
[DERA] I was planning to grab
a bite at Jin's place,

154
00:08:13,030 --> 00:08:15,330
but they only served me
canned coffee.

155
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:17,290
Here. From Jin.

156
00:08:17,790 --> 00:08:19,540
Asked me to give it to you.

157
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:23,420
[Yuru gasps]

158
00:08:23,960 --> 00:08:26,170
It's that magic painting
of my mom and dad!

159
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:27,470
[RIGHT] Oh?

160
00:08:27,710 --> 00:08:28,930
[YURU] She told me at the manor

161
00:08:29,050 --> 00:08:30,880
she'd find a way
to get this to me.

162
00:08:31,140 --> 00:08:33,140
She really made it happen.

163
00:08:35,510 --> 00:08:36,640
Hmm?

164
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:40,350
She decided to slip in
some paintings of herself, too.

165
00:08:40,480 --> 00:08:41,440
FILTER APPLIED TO EYES

166
00:08:41,560 --> 00:08:42,860
[YURU] Pain in the neck.

167
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:46,190
You said you met with Jin?
At a Kagemori place?

168
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:48,570
Yup. Sorry to say
Asa wasn't there.

169
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:51,820
Which means...
since she wasn't there,

170
00:08:51,950 --> 00:08:53,450
you must have exchanged
information

171
00:08:53,580 --> 00:08:55,200
about my mom and dad.

172
00:08:56,870 --> 00:08:58,870
[ON TV] You just had to
figure it out so quickly,

173
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,830
didn't you? You damn brat.

174
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:04,130
[DERA] Yeah, I get it.

175
00:09:04,420 --> 00:09:07,090
So the fake Asa
is a Zashiki-Warashi.

176
00:09:07,210 --> 00:09:09,010
And now she's being held hostage

177
00:09:09,130 --> 00:09:10,920
along with some of the kids
from the village.

178
00:09:11,050 --> 00:09:13,010
Got any idea which ones
they kidnapped?

179
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:14,050
Don't have a clue.

180
00:09:14,180 --> 00:09:15,390
How many do they have?

181
00:09:15,510 --> 00:09:16,510
Don't have a clue.

182
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:17,720
[Yuru groans]

183
00:09:17,850 --> 00:09:18,810
[sighs]

184
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:20,730
And he mentioned me by name?

185
00:09:20,850 --> 00:09:24,360
I'm sure that doesn't feel good,
considering what's at stake.

186
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:27,770
You'd have to be stupid to just
walk into such an obvious trap.

187
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:31,150
I'll say. He did manage
to capture the fake Asa,

188
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:33,570
so we're dealing
with a Daemon Wielder.

189
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:36,080
We're in a difficult spot here.

190
00:09:36,620 --> 00:09:39,040
[YURU] I vote we let
the bandits go in first.

191
00:09:39,160 --> 00:09:41,580
[DERA] Sounds like they're
itchin' for a fight anyway.

192
00:09:41,710 --> 00:09:44,920
Should be easy to let those
hot heads take the bait for us.

193
00:09:45,210 --> 00:09:47,840
Best case scenario,
we get lucky with the timing.

194
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:50,840
Maybe we can rescue the kids
while they duke it out.

195
00:09:50,970 --> 00:09:55,300
I suppose we can save her, too,
fake Asa.

196
00:09:55,430 --> 00:09:58,390
But only because it'll help me
to track down Danji.

197
00:09:59,350 --> 00:10:01,930
I'll find them both
and squeeze them for info

198
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:03,270
on the village.

199
00:10:03,390 --> 00:10:04,310
-They might even know...
-[Right giggles]

200
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:06,400
...something
about my mom and dad.

201
00:10:06,520 --> 00:10:08,690
Hey, what's the big idea,
laughing at me?

202
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:15,950
Didn't you say we're probably
dealing with a Daemon Wielder?

203
00:10:16,070 --> 00:10:17,370
That means we should be able

204
00:10:17,490 --> 00:10:19,700
to detect his location
with Left and Right.

205
00:10:20,330 --> 00:10:22,790
We could even trick him,
place you two somewhere,

206
00:10:22,910 --> 00:10:24,370
so he thinks I'm nearby.

207
00:10:24,750 --> 00:10:25,960
[DERA] Yeah, good idea.

208
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,960
We can send them
into warehouse one first

209
00:10:28,090 --> 00:10:29,040
to intercept.

210
00:10:30,170 --> 00:10:31,630
What about us?

211
00:10:31,760 --> 00:10:33,340
Somewhere in range with my bow.

212
00:10:33,470 --> 00:10:35,720
Sure. There's a factory
across from the warehouse.

213
00:10:36,220 --> 00:10:37,890
Comparatively, how tall is it?

214
00:10:38,010 --> 00:10:40,510
The factory's a little higher up
than the warehouse.

215
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:42,680
-[YURU] That's perfect...
-[KEN] Ms. Hana, what is this?

216
00:10:42,810 --> 00:10:43,810
Don't care.

217
00:10:44,180 --> 00:10:45,690
And if you don't wanna
get dragged into their bullshit,

218
00:10:45,810 --> 00:10:46,730
you shouldn't either.

219
00:10:46,850 --> 00:10:48,230
[RIGHT] Mmm...

220
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:50,940
I'm a mite loathe to be far
from our master's side.

221
00:10:51,070 --> 00:10:52,860
Do you feel it's safe?

222
00:10:53,110 --> 00:10:54,150
I'll get out of there

223
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:56,030
if anything dangerous
comes my way.

224
00:10:56,700 --> 00:10:58,780
I'm not planning to be a hero.

225
00:10:58,910 --> 00:11:00,370
I'll be counting on you.

226
00:11:00,490 --> 00:11:01,830
DAEMONS OF THE SHADOW REALM

227
00:11:01,950 --> 00:11:03,700
[birds chirping]

228
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:06,000
I want to see my brother.

229
00:11:07,670 --> 00:11:09,630
I want to see my brother.

230
00:11:10,130 --> 00:11:11,300
Should we be worried

231
00:11:11,550 --> 00:11:13,920
that she's repeating
the same sentence over and over?

232
00:11:14,050 --> 00:11:16,880
-I want to see my brother.
-[GABBY] Yep, she's broken.

233
00:11:17,010 --> 00:11:18,550
[HAGURE] Well, I guess it's okay

234
00:11:18,680 --> 00:11:20,930
as long as her hands
are still moving.

235
00:11:21,050 --> 00:11:22,220
No, not okay.

236
00:11:22,350 --> 00:11:24,230
All the background
characters are Yuru.

237
00:11:24,850 --> 00:11:26,060
Mm...

238
00:11:26,180 --> 00:11:27,060
STUDIO OUTSIDER

239
00:11:27,190 --> 00:11:28,440
Why don't we take
a little break?

240
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:29,610
[ALL] Sounds good.

241
00:11:32,650 --> 00:11:34,860
[HAGURE] Would you like
some tea, Tachikawa?

242
00:11:34,990 --> 00:11:37,740
[Tachikawa crying]

243
00:11:37,860 --> 00:11:39,950
Your stories are all so sweet!

244
00:11:40,070 --> 00:11:41,580
I don't know how you do it!

245
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:44,330
So glad to hear
you like my work! Hooray!

246
00:11:44,450 --> 00:11:45,460
For real, though.

247
00:11:45,910 --> 00:11:48,080
It's kinda crazy you can create
beautiful stuff like that

248
00:11:48,210 --> 00:11:50,130
when you come
from such a bloodthirsty family.

249
00:11:50,250 --> 00:11:53,630
[HAGURE] It's because
my family's so bloodthirsty.

250
00:11:53,750 --> 00:11:57,420
I just drew the idyllic world
I wished I could live in, and...

251
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:00,470
-folks liked it.
-[NARRATOR] Hikaru Hagure

252
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:03,430
is a master of heartfelt,
happy manga.

253
00:12:04,760 --> 00:12:05,810
It hurts my soul

254
00:12:06,230 --> 00:12:08,060
to live a life where things
like vengeance, betrayal,

255
00:12:08,190 --> 00:12:10,270
and cold-blooded murder
are basically normal.

256
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:12,480
Hey, for the record,
I've never killed anyone!

257
00:12:12,610 --> 00:12:13,570
Me neither!

258
00:12:13,690 --> 00:12:15,280
[HAGURE]
Then it's not too late.

259
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:18,240
You two could quit
and get legitimate jobs.

260
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:20,530
[HARUO] Yeah, but working here,
I've got a boss

261
00:12:20,660 --> 00:12:22,910
who literally cleans up
my messes if I screw up.

262
00:12:23,030 --> 00:12:24,030
That's hard to beat.

263
00:12:24,490 --> 00:12:26,710
[TACHIKAWA] Plus it pays well,
and I really need the money.

264
00:12:26,830 --> 00:12:27,910
[HAGURE] Hmm...

265
00:12:28,660 --> 00:12:30,120
Fair enough.

266
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:32,710
I just hate that in our world,

267
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:35,300
people who could otherwise
have lived ordinary lives

268
00:12:35,420 --> 00:12:37,840
are forced
to bloody their hands.

269
00:12:37,970 --> 00:12:39,720
It's not right.

270
00:12:40,430 --> 00:12:42,350
So here's a solution for you.

271
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:44,680
Become the clan head
and then you can fire us.

272
00:12:44,810 --> 00:12:47,230
Don't wanna! I'm always
saying I have no desire

273
00:12:47,350 --> 00:12:49,100
to lead this shady family.

274
00:12:49,230 --> 00:12:50,390
Wait, here's an idea.

275
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:52,810
Why don't you two become
pro manga assistants

276
00:12:52,940 --> 00:12:54,730
and work in my studio instead?

277
00:12:54,860 --> 00:12:56,400
[TACHIKAWA]
I have zero artistic talent.

278
00:12:56,530 --> 00:12:57,490
[HARUO] It's not nice to poach

279
00:12:57,610 --> 00:12:59,150
other people's employees,
you know.

280
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:00,900
I'm no good with manga stuff,

281
00:13:01,030 --> 00:13:02,570
but if you ever
need anything else,

282
00:13:02,700 --> 00:13:03,910
then just say the word.

283
00:13:04,030 --> 00:13:05,240
My siblings and I'll help.

284
00:13:05,370 --> 00:13:07,500
We owe the Kagemori clan
big time.

285
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:09,870
[TACHIKAWA] You have siblings?
I didn't know that.

286
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,380
Yep. Natsuki is the eldest.

287
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:13,920
Then there's Fuyuki.

288
00:13:14,040 --> 00:13:17,250
I'm third in line.
And Akio's the baby.

289
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:19,880
All the Kuroya siblings
at your service.

290
00:13:20,010 --> 00:13:22,220
[TACHIKAWA] Four of you?
Man, that's a lot.

291
00:13:22,680 --> 00:13:24,850
[HARUO] Yeah.
We're not related by blood,

292
00:13:24,970 --> 00:13:27,390
but we were in the same
care home together, so...

293
00:13:27,510 --> 00:13:28,480
[TACHIKAWA] Sorry.

294
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:30,600
I get if you don't want
to talk about it.

295
00:13:30,730 --> 00:13:31,980
I was being nosy.

296
00:13:32,100 --> 00:13:33,690
Not at all. It's fine.

297
00:13:34,860 --> 00:13:36,860
We were all abandoned as babies.

298
00:13:36,980 --> 00:13:38,740
Left on the doorstep
of a nursery

299
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:40,240
run by the Kagemoris.

300
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:43,530
How could any-bunny not love
such an adorable little face?

301
00:13:43,660 --> 00:13:44,780
Oh, wow.

302
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:47,870
I had no idea the Kagemoris were
in the childcare business.

303
00:13:47,990 --> 00:13:49,450
We run an orphanage, too.

304
00:13:49,580 --> 00:13:52,040
My dad's a bit of a softie
when it comes to kids.

305
00:13:52,160 --> 00:13:53,120
Just them, though.

306
00:13:53,420 --> 00:13:55,830
[TACHIKAWA] Surely
that's not all there is to it.

307
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,000
I mean, with your family,

308
00:13:57,130 --> 00:13:59,210
there must be
an ulterior motive, right?

309
00:13:59,340 --> 00:14:00,670
I guess so.

310
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:03,180
I'm sure a lot of our
charitable work is performative,

311
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:05,550
letting the public see
our good side and all that.

312
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:08,010
[HARUO] Yeah, look at me
and my siblings.

313
00:14:08,140 --> 00:14:09,680
They took us all in,

314
00:14:09,810 --> 00:14:11,890
and they brought us up
to be foot soldiers

315
00:14:12,020 --> 00:14:13,270
in their evil clan.

316
00:14:13,390 --> 00:14:14,350
[laughing]

317
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:15,770
[Natsuki sighs]

318
00:14:17,230 --> 00:14:18,730
I want out.

319
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:21,240
What are you looking at,
Natsuki?

320
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:22,450
A matchmaking site.

321
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:24,610
I really want to quit.

322
00:14:25,070 --> 00:14:27,450
Hmm. We've got work.

323
00:14:28,160 --> 00:14:30,370
The master and Jin
are plotting something.

324
00:14:35,670 --> 00:14:37,250
Here. Know the way?

325
00:14:37,380 --> 00:14:38,670
I think so.

326
00:14:40,050 --> 00:14:42,340
What's up? Is Gabby headed out
somewhere?

327
00:14:42,470 --> 00:14:44,630
Yeah. With Natsuki,
Fuyuki, and the master.

328
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:47,220
Now, listen closely.
This is important.

329
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:50,510
[AKIO] It's unusual for her
to leave the manor without Asa.

330
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:52,680
[HARUO]
Asa is currently non-functional.

331
00:14:52,810 --> 00:14:55,980
They're scared she'll screw up,
so they're going without her.

332
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:57,100
Where to?

333
00:14:57,230 --> 00:14:58,310
[HARUO] Hmm?

334
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:01,650
The Fujimurayama warehouses.

335
00:15:01,940 --> 00:15:04,280
We got word about a move
against Yuru.

336
00:15:08,580 --> 00:15:09,660
[Yuru exhales]

337
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:12,040
[YURU] It's the full moon.

338
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:16,080
And the hour of the Boar
is in about two hours.

339
00:15:18,630 --> 00:15:20,040
Dera's ready.

340
00:15:20,170 --> 00:15:22,500
And Left and Right
are in position.

341
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:31,510
No sign of the enemy yet.

342
00:15:34,520 --> 00:15:36,180
Are the bandits here?

343
00:15:36,310 --> 00:15:38,810
Could they be lying in wait
somewhere?

344
00:15:38,940 --> 00:15:39,900
[grunts]

345
00:15:41,150 --> 00:15:42,570
[grunts softly]

346
00:15:44,610 --> 00:15:47,240
[growls]

347
00:15:52,830 --> 00:15:53,990
[Yuru grunts]

348
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:58,000
How? Where did
this thing come from?

349
00:15:58,750 --> 00:16:00,460
I didn't sense anything.

350
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:02,670
It didn't even make a sound!

351
00:16:03,630 --> 00:16:05,000
[grunting softly]

352
00:16:14,470 --> 00:16:16,640
[growls]

353
00:16:17,350 --> 00:16:19,020
[Yuru exhales]

354
00:16:20,610 --> 00:16:22,570
Dera hasn't noticed it yet.

355
00:16:23,900 --> 00:16:25,690
Neither have Left and Right.

356
00:16:26,690 --> 00:16:30,280
Which means...
it's totally undetectable.

357
00:16:30,620 --> 00:16:32,240
There's no bloodlust.

358
00:16:32,370 --> 00:16:33,780
But one quick twist of my neck,

359
00:16:33,910 --> 00:16:36,080
and I'd be dead
before I could react.

360
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:37,580
[exhales]

361
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:40,790
If I called out to them
right now,

362
00:16:40,920 --> 00:16:43,420
who'd be able to help me
out of this the fastest?

363
00:16:43,540 --> 00:16:46,090
Simple. I'm your guardian, kid.

364
00:16:46,210 --> 00:16:48,670
Plus, your cute little sister
told me to watch your back.

365
00:16:49,130 --> 00:16:50,260
[Yuru grunts softly]

366
00:16:50,510 --> 00:16:52,760
[YURU] Guess I'm putting
my faith in you.

367
00:16:54,050 --> 00:16:56,430
Dera, shoot this thing!

368
00:16:56,560 --> 00:16:57,640
[gasps]

369
00:16:58,980 --> 00:17:00,060
[DERA] What is that?

370
00:17:01,310 --> 00:17:02,900
When did it get here?

371
00:17:10,110 --> 00:17:11,200
[Dera gasps]

372
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:25,960
[Dera gasps, grunts]

373
00:17:29,670 --> 00:17:30,630
[DERA] Yuru!

374
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:32,380
Where are Left and Right?

375
00:17:33,220 --> 00:17:34,680
[Right growls]

376
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:35,930
[grunts]

377
00:17:37,020 --> 00:17:38,560
[RIGHT] 'Tis like hitting air.

378
00:17:46,320 --> 00:17:47,530
[grunts]

379
00:17:51,700 --> 00:17:53,410
[grunting]

380
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,340
[yells]

381
00:18:17,260 --> 00:18:19,350
[spits] 'Tis a bit smaller.

382
00:18:19,470 --> 00:18:20,600
Merely a bit.

383
00:18:21,060 --> 00:18:24,020
[RIGHT] Then we'll have
to tear it apart piece by piece.

384
00:18:24,140 --> 00:18:26,520
[LEFT] Not how
I prefer to do battle.

385
00:18:26,650 --> 00:18:27,730
[both grunt]

386
00:18:30,860 --> 00:18:32,150
[Right grunts]

387
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:33,610
[both gasp]

388
00:18:36,570 --> 00:18:37,870
[RIGHT] They're gone?

389
00:18:51,300 --> 00:18:53,550
Young Yuru! Good evening!

390
00:18:53,670 --> 00:18:54,760
[Yuru grunts softly]

391
00:18:55,260 --> 00:18:56,550
[YURU] Asuma Kagemo...

392
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:58,010
[groans]

393
00:18:58,140 --> 00:19:00,560
[ASUMA] Oh, I'm sorry.
Are you motion sick?

394
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:01,810
[Yuru grunts softly]

395
00:19:01,930 --> 00:19:04,350
This thing...
Is it your other daemon?

396
00:19:04,890 --> 00:19:08,310
Indeed! Together,
they are Kin'u-gyokuto.

397
00:19:08,560 --> 00:19:10,400
This one is named Yozakura.

398
00:19:10,690 --> 00:19:13,400
I'm genuinely impressed
by how undetectable they are.

399
00:19:13,530 --> 00:19:14,400
[Asuma giggles]

400
00:19:14,530 --> 00:19:15,780
[YURU] Where's the other?

401
00:19:15,900 --> 00:19:17,410
[ASUMA] You refer to Asagiri.

402
00:19:17,530 --> 00:19:18,950
I'm afraid
they're weak at night,

403
00:19:19,080 --> 00:19:20,280
so they won't be joining us.

404
00:19:20,410 --> 00:19:23,120
Conversely, Yozakura
doesn't like the day,

405
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:25,410
so they try
to only operate at night.

406
00:19:26,120 --> 00:19:27,420
[YURU] Hmm.

407
00:19:27,540 --> 00:19:30,170
So I could take them
when it's light out. Noted.

408
00:19:30,670 --> 00:19:32,840
[SHINGO]
This brat gives me the creeps.

409
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:34,550
You're alone in enemy territory.

410
00:19:34,670 --> 00:19:36,930
How are you calm enough
to make small talk?

411
00:19:37,630 --> 00:19:40,260
Better not let him see
my daemons yet.

412
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:42,100
You idiot.

413
00:19:42,350 --> 00:19:44,560
Go and tell the whole world
about your daemon's weaknesses,

414
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:45,890
why don't you?

415
00:19:46,020 --> 00:19:47,520
It's a show of good faith.

416
00:19:47,640 --> 00:19:49,730
We would like him to trust us.

417
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:53,110
If you want my trust,
then answer honestly.

418
00:19:53,230 --> 00:19:54,230
Are you after Seal?

419
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:56,860
It is as I told you
back at the manor.

420
00:19:56,990 --> 00:19:59,320
I believe those with
special powers should be allowed

421
00:19:59,450 --> 00:20:01,240
to live their lives
under the jurisdiction

422
00:20:01,370 --> 00:20:02,790
of suitable overseers.

423
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:03,990
Not independently.

424
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:06,250
[YURU]
The heck is "jurisdiction?"

425
00:20:06,370 --> 00:20:07,960
[ASUMA]
So what do you say, Yuru?

426
00:20:08,080 --> 00:20:09,040
[YURU] Hm?

427
00:20:09,830 --> 00:20:11,040
[Asuma chuckles]

428
00:20:11,170 --> 00:20:13,750
Tell me, would you like to die?

429
00:20:13,880 --> 00:20:15,880
-[running footsteps]
-[panting]

430
00:20:21,260 --> 00:20:23,260
Where is he? In here?

431
00:20:23,390 --> 00:20:25,890
He was kidnapped by that
skull-faced cluster of moths.

432
00:20:26,020 --> 00:20:27,310
Then they vanished here.

433
00:20:27,430 --> 00:20:29,850
What? Are you able
to track Yuru's scent?

434
00:20:30,310 --> 00:20:32,360
[Right groans] I think not.

435
00:20:32,480 --> 00:20:34,440
The tang of blood hangs
too heavy.

436
00:20:34,570 --> 00:20:36,030
'Tis hard to make him out.

437
00:20:36,150 --> 00:20:37,360
[Dera sighs]

438
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:39,320
[switch flips]

439
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:49,580
Good evening to you.

440
00:20:52,540 --> 00:20:54,170
[DERA] Twin katanas.

441
00:20:54,300 --> 00:20:56,380
They're daemons. I see.

442
00:20:56,510 --> 00:20:58,510
You're the guy
the shaman mentioned.

443
00:20:59,130 --> 00:21:00,680
The pervert!

444
00:21:00,800 --> 00:21:01,720
[IVAN] Time out.

445
00:21:01,970 --> 00:21:04,430
How is that the reputation
I got from the guy?

446
00:21:05,390 --> 00:21:07,270
Wow, man, that is brutal.

447
00:21:07,390 --> 00:21:10,020
Not like I love the bandits,
but did you have to kill them?

448
00:21:10,140 --> 00:21:12,060
You mean these pests
in the corners,

449
00:21:12,190 --> 00:21:13,770
trying to interrupt our deal?

450
00:21:13,900 --> 00:21:15,520
None of these people had to die

451
00:21:15,650 --> 00:21:18,150
if Yuru had come alone
like I told him to.

452
00:21:18,530 --> 00:21:20,820
And these must be
the Divine Guardians.

453
00:21:20,950 --> 00:21:22,410
Yuru's daemons.

454
00:21:22,530 --> 00:21:24,830
What I don't get is
why the natural enemies

455
00:21:24,950 --> 00:21:27,700
of Break and Seal would form
a contract with a twin?

456
00:21:28,080 --> 00:21:29,410
Especially you, Left.

457
00:21:29,750 --> 00:21:32,500
Your compatibility
with Seal couldn't be worse.

458
00:21:33,130 --> 00:21:34,630
With you around,

459
00:21:34,750 --> 00:21:38,380
Seal might flat out refuse
to form a contract with Yuru.

460
00:21:38,920 --> 00:21:40,920
Hate to say it, but...

461
00:21:42,630 --> 00:21:45,220
to ensure everything works out,
you gotta die.

462
00:21:45,810 --> 00:21:48,020
[scoffs]
The gentleman wants a duel!

463
00:21:48,140 --> 00:21:49,770
-What say you?
-[bone cracks]

464
00:21:52,810 --> 00:21:54,730
I gladly accept.

465
00:21:54,860 --> 00:21:57,360
[♪ closing theme song playing]

466
00:23:26,610 --> 00:23:27,780
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

467
00:23:27,910 --> 00:23:29,780
[IVAN] To ensure
everything works out,

468
00:23:29,910 --> 00:23:30,910
you gotta die.

469
00:23:31,290 --> 00:23:33,410
[SHINGO] There's no place
for you in Higashi anymore.

470
00:23:33,540 --> 00:23:34,830
[RIGHT] It's Yuru's parents!

471
00:23:34,950 --> 00:23:37,500
I smell the blood
of Mine and Nagisa!

472
00:23:37,620 --> 00:23:39,840
EPISODE 16
KAGEMORI AND SHINGO
